{"title":"Manmohan Singh, RIP","link":"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/909996479/0/marginalrevolution~Manmohan-Singh-RIP.html","date":1735237646000,"content":"<p><span>I am sad to hear about the passing of Manmohan Singh at age 92.</span></p>\r\n<p>Singh was perhaps the most influential Indian policymaker in the last five decades.  An Oxbridge educated trade economist, he became India’s most important technocrat in the 1980s and 1990s – occupying every top position in economic policy –  <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://nam11.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.pmindia.gov.in%2Fen%2Fformer_pm%2Fdr-manmohan-singh-2%2F&amp;data=05%7C02%7Ctcowen%40gmu.edu%7Ccf7efe31d5d046d1e00a08dd25d1dd51%7C9e857255df574c47a0c00546460380cb%7C0%7C0%7C638708305489754083%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=qfXqSGxjX7RybwCG%2FjofWmvNr9EE5i9%2BxsaSjgQiFc8%3D&amp;reserved=0\" target=\"_blank\">finance secretary; deputy chairman of the planning commission; governor of the RBI, and chief economic adviser</a>.  And as finance minister in 1991, when he brought the Indian economy out of socialism to embrace markets and global trade.  After Modi and Nehru, he is also India’s longest continuously serving prime minister over two terms from 2004-2014.</p>\r\n<p>For more about his work and long career in economic policy read <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://nam11.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fglobal.oup.com%2Facademic%2Fproduct%2Fchanging-india-9780199483563%3Fcc%3Dus%26lang%3Den%26&amp;data=05%7C02%7Ctcowen%40gmu.edu%7Ccf7efe31d5d046d1e00a08dd25d1dd51%7C9e857255df574c47a0c00546460380cb%7C0%7C0%7C638708305489773802%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=aLthNoARPn0v2TkYSnVJvXeUdNvaIEDeNdypw6Wp4IE%3D&amp;reserved=0\" target=\"_blank\">Changing India</a> –  a five volume collection on Singh’s work as an academic, policymaker, politician and on the family man, <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://nam11.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.amazon.com%2FStrictly-Personal-Gursharan-Daman-Singh%2Fdp%2F9352643194&amp;data=05%7C02%7Ctcowen%40gmu.edu%7Ccf7efe31d5d046d1e00a08dd25d1dd51%7C9e857255df574c47a0c00546460380cb%7C0%7C0%7C638708305489787602%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=r1y%2FW8r26C6fzGZR9fggagfiE84OuENGQbQehttsvsI%3D&amp;reserved=0\" target=\"_blank\">Strictly Personal</a> by his daughter Daman Singh.  And to learn more about India’s liberalization and economic reforms, follow <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://secure-web.cisco.com/1X7y1dwyTv0JQlZiWueE12cGMSucH6Fkor780BY4INopC8Em8YR3Ww5WnI_WdYnBd9ZiWfheznRn7B_5IJ9NUBmNBs2WshHAIUI44XkNarYoCGJFBrHSY_m8Od_f-X07AmqGIaodbTI59mubcQ-mPZvUdtzPZz50o0_kU2IO0XpdujMOuBEM3wtomco05K0b3nHu_hwqU-guP8PGMY-3hP5XJdqtHv73RRYNaCifMqnuA9fqkdP4VNK-2UNuFlUmYyg64EZJdYfS01MPKHUP4eGNwL_xm0tX3oEQS1Jnk3J9kKtIXIZEkX93IP0z-935uKeghTMZX12kX9TJxS9gWzTLhxQt7BJ6tSqU1VJYAObbubhJyT-1w8psy84hUCMizh9I6dXSsOeXYwR-Si1v3x6yUZb0ebsVNzYncY8INDQ4/https%3A%2F%2Fthe1991project.com%2F\" target=\"_blank\">the 1991 Project </a>at the Mercatus Center led by Shruti Rajagopalan and her team.</p>\r\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2024/12/manmohan-singh-rip.html\">Manmohan Singh, RIP</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com\">Marginal REVOLUTION</a>.</p>\r\n<img height=\"1\" width=\"1\" src=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/i/909996479/0/marginalrevolution\" />\r\n<div><a href